 <rdf:Alt> <rdf:li xml:lang=\""x-default\"">NMIHA-2002-17b.tif</rdf:li> </rdf:Alt> </dc:title> <dc:rights> <rdf:Alt> <rdf:li xml:lang=\""x-default\"">© National Museum of Ireland</rdf:li> </rdf:Alt> </dc:rights> <dc:subject> <rdf:Bag> <rdf:li>objects</rdf:li> <rdf:li>sac_exhib_06</rdf:li> </rdf:Bag> </dc:subject> <dc:description> <rdf:Alt> <rdf:li xml:lang=\""x-default\"">Single barrelled shotgun. These assorted items suggest the difficulty of providing effective weapons to the rural fighters during the War of Independence.  Most farmers owned a shotgun — thus in the countryside they were the most common IRA weapon. When the proper ammunition was not available, cartridge cases would occasionally be refilled with gelignite, leading to accidents. HA:2002.17 (displayed in \""Soldiers &amp; Chiefs\"" exhibition at National Museum of Ireland - Decorative Arts &amp; History)</rdf:li> </rdf:Alt> </dc:description> <xmpMM:History> <rdf:Seq> <rdf:li stEvt:action=\""saved\"" stEvt:instanceID=\""xmp.iid:04FC85AA47206811A6198D13334F7139\"" stEvt:when=\""2010-09-21T19:13:26+01:00\"" stEvt:softwareAgent=\""Adobe Photoshop CS4 Macintosh\"" stEvt:changed=\""/\""/> <rdf:li stEvt:action=\""saved\"" stEvt:instanceID=\""xmp.iid:1A2541031E2068118C148486E5B169BB\"" stEvt:when=\""2016-02-12T12:34:39Z\"" stEvt:softwareAgent=\""Adobe Photoshop CS6 (Macintosh)\"" stEvt:changed=\""/\""/> <rdf:li stEvt:action=\""saved\"" stEvt:instanceID=\""xmp.iid:0106FA4120206811822ADF23585B1F0A\"" stEvt:when=\""2019-10-09T13:04:52+01:00\"" stEvt:softwareAgent=\""Adobe Photoshop Camera Raw 9.1\"" stEvt:changed=\""/metadata\""/> <rdf:li stEvt:action=\""saved\"" stEvt:instanceID=\""xmp.iid:b0f63282-b489-4d13-8d55-d476b55536b1\"" stEvt:when=\""2019-10-09T13:23:10+01:00\"" stEvt:softwareAgent=\""Adobe Photoshop Camera Raw 9.1.1 (Macintosh)\"" stEvt:changed=\""/metadata\""/> <rdf:li stEvt:action=\""saved\"" stEvt:instanceID=\""xmp.iid:78B254AF2C206811822A8E42B21D6E79\"" stEvt:when=\""2019-10-09T15:34:03+01:00\"" s